course: dictionary
lesson: 15026
title: Saying it again
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A restatement is saying or writing something again, often in different or clearer words. The meaning stays the same, but the words change. «Tom said, "The shop is closed on Sundays." Later he said, "You cannot buy anything there on a Sunday."» That is a restatement: the same idea in new words.
explain: Restating a question in your own words helps you understand it. Before you solve a maths problem, try: «So what I need to find is how many sweets are left.» If your restatement matches the question, you are ready to start.
explain: A restatement can also be a new or changed version of a statement, such as a rule or an account. «The club changed its bike rule, so the restatement says bikes must be locked up.» Look for clues like «a restatement of» to spot one.
fact: Restatement means saying or writing something again in different or clearer words.
fact: A restatement is a noun: a restatement, restatements.
fact: A good essay conclusion includes a restatement of the main point.
fact: Phrases you may see are «a restatement of» and «restatement of the question».
fact: In law and business, rules and money figures can be restated, which means they are given in a new version.
exercise: «Tom said, "The shop is closed on Sundays." Later he said, "You cannot buy anything there on a Sunday."» What is the second sentence? | A list of prices | *A restatement of the first | A question about shops | A shout of anger
exercise: Mia writes, «So I need to find how many sweets are left.» What is she doing? | Writing a poem | Ignoring the question | *Restating the question in her own words | Counting the sweets twice
exercise: Which word means saying something again in clearer words? | Volcano | Blanket | Puddle | *Restatement
test: In an essay, a conclusion with «a restatement of the main point» does what? | *Gives the main idea again in new words | Lists the spellings of hard words | Adds a brand new idea at the end | Removes the main idea
test: A club changes its rule and writes a new version of it. What is this new version? | A dinner menu | *A restatement of the rule | A puddle | A whisper
exam: Which sentence is a restatement of «Rain stopped the match, so we went home»? | It was a sunny day at the match | We played the match in the rain | Nobody went home that day | *The match ended early because of the rain, so we went home
